            H3("Environments and release windows"),
            "Plan which environments exist (development, test, pre-production, production), who controls them and when they are available. Environment shortages are a common cause of slipped test cycles. Find out early when the organisation allows production changes, which periods are frozen (for example financial year-end) and how far ahead the change authority needs requests. These windows become hard constraints in the schedule.",
            H3("Data migration"),
            "Treat migration as a workstream with its own plan: profile the source data, agree mappings and cleansing rules with data owners, build repeatable scripts, then rehearse the full migration several times. Each rehearsal should measure three things: whether every extracted record is accounted for (loaded or rejected with a reason), the reject rate by data type and the elapsed load time. The worked example below shows how those measures feed the cutover plan.",
