            H3("Security and data protection"),
            "Bring information security in at design, not at go-live. Under UK GDPR Article 35, a data protection impact assessment (DPIA) must be carried out before processing begins where a type of processing, in particular using new technologies, is likely to result in a high risk to individuals. The Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) advises doing one if in doubt, and notes that its DPIA guidance is under review following the Data (Use and Access) Act. Record privacy and security risks in the [risk register](/project-management/risk-register/) with owners and responses, just like schedule risks.",
