            "Software for IT project management",
            "IT organisations usually combine three kinds of tool: an IT service management (ITSM) platform for incidents, requests and change records; a developer tool for code, issues and releases; and a project or portfolio platform to plan projects, manage resources across teams and report to leadership.",
            "For the project and portfolio layer, look for request intake forms, Gantt and board views of the same work, dependencies and milestones, resource planning across projects, portfolio dashboards and integrations with ITSM and developer tools. [Wrike](/project-management-tools/wrike/) is the strongest all-in-one option in [our tool rankings](/project-management-tools/) for this role, with request forms, Gantt charts, resource planning and two-way sync with tools such as Jira and GitHub. Engineering-heavy teams often run development work in [Jira](/project-management-tools/jira/), which suits Scrum and Kanban but lacks a classic Gantt chart with critical path and baselines, so plan-driven IT projects usually pair it with a planning tool.",
